Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: keep a surface's contents across a write-only D3D9 lock

A WriteOnly lock without Discard mapped the GPU texture write-only, and
the unmap uploaded the whole box from a staging copy that never held the
surface's contents, so every texel the caller did not write was lost.
DirectDraw's emulation layer does exactly that for blits the HAL does not
offer (colour key, mirror): it locks the whole destination write-only and
writes only the blitted rectangle. Such locks now take the readback path,
which starts from the current contents.

Evidence: docs/dxdiag.md, docs/evidence/dxdiag/ (ddcaps blit checks).
Origin: vmlab-win3d, worker fix-dxdiag.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Resource.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Resource.cpp
index 7c5554c..6f27d53 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Resource.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Resource.cpp
@@ -3350,10 +3350,19 @@ D3D9Lock(HANDLE hDevice, D3DDDIARG_LOCK *data)
           !D3D9UploadSubResource(device, resource, subresource_index))
          return E_NOTIMPL;
 
-      if ((usage & PIPE_MAP_READ) && D3D9PoolNeedsReadback(resource->pool)) {
+      /* A write-only lock without Discard still has to keep the texels the
+       * caller does not write.  DirectDraw's emulation layer relies on that:
+       * for a colour-key or mirror blit the HAL does not offer, it locks
+       * the whole destination write-only and stores only the blitted
+       * rectangle.  A plain write map of a GPU texture uploads the whole
+       * box from an uninitialised staging copy, so such locks go through
+       * the readback path, which starts from the current contents. */
+      const bool preserve_contents =
+         (usage & PIPE_MAP_READ) || !(usage & PIPE_MAP_DISCARD_RANGE);
+      if (preserve_contents && D3D9PoolNeedsReadback(resource->pool)) {
          map = D3D9ReadbackTextureLock(device, resource, sub,
-                                       subresource_index, usage, &box,
-                                       data);
+                                       subresource_index,
+                                       usage | PIPE_MAP_READ, &box, data);
       } else {
          if (!device->pipe->texture_map)
             return E_NOTIMPL;
